iio: frequency: admv1013: use dev in admv1013_properties_parse()

Stable commit 417e1fb55a791 ("iio: frequency: admv1013: add dev variable") and
the following property-parsing cleanup (merged without conflict) removes the local 'struct spi_device *spi = st->spi'
from admv1013_properties_parse() and uses 'dev' instead. The downstream-only
clock-scale lookup at the end of the function (of_clk_get_scale()) still uses
'spi', which no longer exists. Use dev->of_node, which is the same node.

diff --git a/drivers/iio/frequency/admv1013.c b/drivers/iio/frequency/admv1013.c
--- a/drivers/iio/frequency/admv1013.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/frequency/admv1013.c
@@ -566,7 +566,7 @@
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	return of_clk_get_scale(spi->dev.of_node, NULL, &st->clkscale);
+	return of_clk_get_scale(dev->of_node, NULL, &st->clkscale);
 }
 
 static int admv1013_probe(struct spi_device *spi)
